WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.981
Veteran Suicide.

00:00:01.931 --> 00:00:06.454
Male veterans die by suicide at one point four times the civilian rate.

00:00:06.454 --> 00:00:09.569
Female veterans at one point nine times.

00:00:09.569 --> 00:00:13.238
This elevated risk has persisted for forty-two years.

00:00:13.238 --> 00:00:16.011
The government has known for four decades.

00:00:16.011 --> 00:00:22.749
When veterans called Veterans Affairs asking for mental health support, at least four confirmed cases were offered MAID instead.

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:24.124
The data.

00:00:24.124 --> 00:00:31.659
Veterans Affairs Canada's own mortality study covers forty-two years of data from 1976 to 2018.

00:00:31.659 --> 00:00:37.056
The finding: veteran suicide risk is persistently elevated across the entire period.

00:00:37.056 --> 00:00:40.124
It does not decline with time after service.

00:00:40.124 --> 00:00:44.647
Male veterans die by suicide at one point four times the civilian rate.

00:00:44.647 --> 00:00:47.762
Female veterans at one point nine times.

00:00:47.762 --> 00:00:51.863
This is not a new discovery — the government has known for decades.

00:00:51.863 --> 00:00:53.874
The MAID intersection.

00:00:53.874 --> 00:00:57.147
A Paralympian veteran asked for a wheelchair ramp.

00:00:57.147 --> 00:01:00.465
Veterans Affairs responded: we can help you die.

00:01:00.465 --> 00:01:07.374
At least four to five confirmed cases of veterans being offered MAID by VAC employees when calling for mental health support.

00:01:07.374 --> 00:01:10.931
A MAID procedure costs twenty-five hundred dollars.

00:01:10.931 --> 00:01:14.181
A wheelchair ramp costs three to eight thousand.

00:01:14.181 --> 00:01:18.204
Annual disability benefits cost fifteen to forty thousand.

00:01:18.204 --> 00:01:22.068
It is cheaper to kill a veteran than to provide a ramp for two years.

00:01:22.068 --> 00:01:24.329
The veteran-to-MAID pipeline.

00:01:24.329 --> 00:01:28.454
Inadequate transition support leads to denied disability claims.

00:01:28.454 --> 00:01:31.579
Denied claims lead to untreated conditions.

00:01:31.579 --> 00:01:34.306
Untreated conditions lead to crisis.

00:01:34.306 --> 00:01:37.386
Crisis leads to a call to Veterans Affairs.

00:01:37.386 --> 00:01:39.818
Veterans Affairs offers MAID.

00:01:39.818 --> 00:01:44.136
The pipeline is documented at every stage by the government's own data.

00:01:44.136 --> 00:01:46.534
This is not random failure.

00:01:46.534 --> 00:01:49.499
It is a connected chain from service to death.
